      "preview": "חַח: gancho, argola, grilhão.",
      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חַח</span></big>  <strong>substantivo masculino: gancho, argola, grilhão</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">חַח</span> absoluto <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:22\" href=\"/Exodus.35.22\">Ex 35:22</a>; com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">חַחִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 37:29\" href=\"/Isaiah.37.29\">Is 37:29</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 19:28\" href=\"/II_Kings.19.28\">2 K 19:28</a>; plural <span dir=\"rtl\">חַחִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 19:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.19.4\">Ez 19:4</a> + 2 vezes + <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 29:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.29.4\">Ez 29:4</a> Qere (Ketib errôneo <span dir=\"rtl\">חחיים</span>, ver abaixo);—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>gancho, argola</em>, no nariz do cativo <span dir=\"rtl\">וְשַׂמְתִּי חַחִי בְּאַפֶּ֑ךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 37:29\" href=\"/Isaiah.37.29\">Is 37:29</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Kings 19:28\" href=\"/II_Kings.19.28\">2 K 19:28</a> (cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּחֹחִים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 33:11\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.33.11\">2 Ch 33:11</a>, ver <a data-ref=\"BDB, חוֹחַ\" href=\"/BDB,_חוֹחַ\", dir=\"rtl\">חוֹחַ</a> acima); assim de príncipes de Judá, sob figura de leões novos <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 19:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.19.4\">Ez 19:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 19:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.19.9\">9</a> (em v. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 19:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.19.9\">9</a> transpor, de modo que <span dir=\"rtl\">בחחים</span> siga <span dir=\"rtl\">הביא</span> como v. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 19:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.19.4\">4</a>; assim Co); nas mandíbulas do crocodilo (metáfora de Faraó), com <span dir=\"rtl\">נתן</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 29:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.29.4\">Ez 29:4</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 38:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.38.4\">38:4</a> (mas 𝔊 omite e o sentido se opõe, cf. Co e—duvidosamente—Da).<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>gancho, argola</em> como ornamento, talvez <em>argola nasal</em> (outros <em>broche</em>, ver VB), <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:22\" href=\"/Exodus.35.22\">Ex 35:22</a> (P; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">נֶזֶם</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">טַבַּעַת</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">כּוּמָז</span>).",
